-- 265: the key scope 'partner_read_all'. Like 'partner_push' (an outside creative partner bound to ONE vendor: pushes tickets and creative links for that vendor, nothing else is writable) but it may also READ
-- every route the app serves except the secret-bearing ones (API key admin, saved-view tokens, vendor link tokens, the brain key; app/api_keys.py SECRET_BLOCKED). It is a deliberate per-key choice:
-- python -m etl.api_keys create --scope partner_read_all --vendor <Vendor>, or set-scope on an existing partner key. Additive and idempotent; existing keys are unchanged.
ALTER TABLE api_keys DROP CONSTRAINT IF EXISTS api_keys_scope_check;
ALTER TABLE api_keys ADD CONSTRAINT api_keys_scope_check CHECK (scope IN ('read_assign', 'partner_push', 'partner_read_all'));
ALTER TABLE api_keys DROP CONSTRAINT IF EXISTS api_keys_vendor_scope_check;
ALTER TABLE api_keys ADD CONSTRAINT api_keys_vendor_scope_check CHECK ((scope IN ('partner_push', 'partner_read_all')) = (vendor IS NOT NULL));

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- comments
COMMENT ON TABLE public.api_keys IS 'Scoped API keys for the Tag Explorer API: one row per key handed to a colleague (read_assign: reads everything the app serves, assigns on the production board) or to an outside creative partner (partner_push: bound to one vendor, pushes tickets and creative links, reads only the creative and performance data; partner_read_all: the same writes, and reads everything except secret-bearing routes). Grain: one row per key (id is the primary key; name and key_hash are each unique). Source: python -m etl.api_keys create / revoke (etl/api_keys.py); last_used_at is touched by the web app (app/api_keys.py). Refresh: on demand (a person creates or revokes a key; last_used_at moves at most once a minute while a key is in use). Coverage: from the day the migration was deployed. Caveats: Only the sha256 hash of the key is stored. The key itself is shown once when it is made and cannot be recovered; make a new key and revoke the old one instead. | A revoked key is never deleted, so the history stays. Assignments made with a key carry created_by / updated_by ''key:<name>'' in creative_priorities_assignments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.api_keys.scope IS 'What the key may do. ''read_assign'': every GET, plus five writes on the production board (assign, create tickets, edit, move, comment). ''partner_push'': an outside creative partner, bound to one vendor; pushes tickets and creative links for that vendor, looks at tickets and reads the creative and performance data only. ''partner_read_all'': the same writes as partner_push, and it may also read every route and the data brain except the secret-bearing ones (saved-view and vendor link tokens, the brain key).';
